    {
      "id": "claim_3e07b9ebd2d543bfab35b8b22343a03a",
      "statement": "Theme values are defined twice, in two colour spaces, for two consumers: global.css provides the full oklch `--color-*` token set under `@variant light` and `@variant dark` that makes Uniwind `className` utilities resolve, while lib/theme.ts holds a separate hsl palette and maps only six colours (background, border, card, notification, primary, text) into the React Navigation `Theme` object consumed by the root provider; the chart and sidebar tokens in global.css are consumed by no component.",
